    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n56648" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέντρ-ων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ωνος</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one that bears the marks of the</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέντρον</span>, <i>a rogue that has been
				put to the torture</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				329
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				450
			</span></i> (anap.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>piece of patch-work, rag</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Bito
				55.4
			</span></i>, Herasap.<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				13.1044
			</span></i>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				449
			</span></i>; perh.<i>pen-wiper,</i>
